<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RecallCraft MSI (WiX Toolset v5: `dotnet tool install -g wix`, plus its UI and Util extensions:
  `wix extension add -g WixToolset.UI.wixext/5.0.2` and the same for WixToolset.Util.wixext).
  Built by package.ps1:

    wix build recallcraft.wxs -arch x64 -ext WixToolset.UI.wixext -ext WixToolset.Util.wixext
      -d Version=1.2.3 -d BinDir=... -d IconPath=... -d LicenseRtf=... -o out.msi

  The program (recallcraft.exe: the service, its window and the worker that writes speech down),
  the command-line program (recallcraft-cli.exe) and the speech model in models\ beside them, with
  a Start Menu shortcut for the program. It starts at sign-in for the person who installs it (the
  Run value below). The installer shows the standard WiX look: the license with the choice of who
  it's for, progress, and a finish page.

  One package, two ways to install it (a "dual-purpose" package, Windows Installer 5.0):
  - for everyone on this PC (per-machine): Program Files\RecallCraft, the all-users Start menu,
    HKLM. An administrator has to allow it (UAC). This is the default: `msiexec /i x.msi`,
    `/passive` and `/qn` all install per-machine.
  - just for me (per-user): %LocalAppData%\Programs\RecallCraft, my own Start menu, HKCU. No
    administrator. The installer's first page offers it; on the command line it is
    `msiexec /i x.msi ALLUSERS=2 MSIINSTALLPERUSER=1` (both: the package's own ALLUSERS is 1, and
    Windows reads MSIINSTALLPERUSER only when ALLUSERS is 2).
  The files go under ProgramFiles6432Folder, which Windows points at %LocalAppData%\Programs for a
  per-user install, and the App Paths value is HKMU, which is HKLM per-machine and HKCU per-user.
  An install keeps its scope: Windows upgrades only a product installed the same way, so the first
  page offers only the earlier install's scope when there is one, and a silent install in the
  other scope stops with a message.

  Starting at sign-in is always per person (HKCU), in both scopes, unlike ScreenGrabCraft's
  installer: RecallCraft records the microphone and what the computer plays, so it must never
  start recording for somebody on this PC who hasn't started it themselves; and its own "Start
  RecallCraft when I sign in" switch (crates/desktop/src/service.rs) reads and removes exactly that
  HKCU value, so an HKLM one would bring it back after the owner turned it off. Anyone else on the
  PC gets the same entry the first time they start RecallCraft (the program arranges it on its
  first run, and the advertised shortcut writes this package's per-user part for them).

  UpgradeCode and the component GUIDs below belong to RecallCraft alone. Never copy them from (or
  into) a sibling Craft app: Windows Installer treats every package sharing an UpgradeCode as one
  product, so a shared code makes one app's installer refuse to install ("a newer version is
  already installed") or silently uninstall the other. packaging-lint.yml checks this file has no
  GUID twice.
-->
<Wix xmlns="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxs"
    xmlns:ui="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxs/ui"
    xmlns:util="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxs/util">
  <Package
      Name="RecallCraft"
      Manufacturer="RecallCraft contributors"
      Version="$(var.Version)"
      UpgradeCode="6A0048D5-E5B6-4588-940F-668CA198836D"
      Scope="perMachine"
      Compressed="yes"
      Language="1033">
    <SummaryInformation Description="RecallCraft keeps the last two days of what was said and writes calls down" Manufacturer="RecallCraft contributors" />
    <!-- Same-version upgrades let successive pre-releases of one X.Y.Z replace each other
         (MSI versions are numeric, so 1.2.3-rc.1 and 1.2.3-rc.2 are both 1.2.3). -->
    <MajorUpgrade AllowSameVersionUpgrades="yes"
        DowngradeErrorMessage="A newer version of RecallCraft is already installed." />
    <MediaTemplate EmbedCab="yes" CompressionLevel="high" />

    <Icon Id="RecallCraftIcon.ico" SourceFile="$(var.IconPath)" />
    <Property Id="ARPPRODUCTICON" Value="RecallCraftIcon.ico" />
    <Property Id="ARPURLINFOABOUT" Value="https://github.com/billsecond/recallcraft" />
    <Property Id="ARPURLUPDATEINFO" Value="https://github.com/billsecond/recallcraft/releases" />
    <Property Id="ARPHELPLINK" Value="https://github.com/billsecond/recallcraft/issues" />

    <!-- The service runs all the time (tray icon, the recorder, the replay shortcut):
         recallcraft.exe started with its background flag (the Run value below; XML comments
         can't spell the flag's double hyphen) is a small supervisor that runs the service and
         restarts it if it exits abnormally; the service starts its window and the worker that
         writes speech down as copies of the same program. An upgrade or an uninstall must close
         them all, or their files stay in use and Windows asks for a reboot. WixCloseApplications
         (Util extension, before InstallValidate) sends WM_CLOSE to the windows of every
         recallcraft.exe, on which the window closes; whatever is still running after the timeout
         (the service, whose windows are hidden, the worker and the windowless supervisor) is
         terminated, with exit code 0 so a supervisor that is still there sees a normal end and
         doesn't restart the service. The recording loses at most its last second (it's flushed
         every second). Never a reboot prompt. Only when the program is already installed (repair,
         uninstall) or an older version is being replaced: a first install leaves a portable copy
         alone.
         The Util extension sequences this before InstallFiles, which on an uninstall comes after
         RemoveFiles: the terminating half (a deferred action) would then run after the files it
         holds were due to go, and the uninstall would need a reboot. It is moved to the start of
         the install script instead, ahead of every removal. (It can't go before InstallInitialize:
         it schedules a deferred action.) -->
    <util:CloseApplication Id="CloseRecallCraft" Target="recallcraft.exe"
        CloseMessage="yes" TerminateProcess="0" RebootPrompt="no"
        Condition="Installed OR WIX_UPGRADE_DETECTED" />
    <InstallExecuteSequence>
      <Custom Action="override Wix4CloseApplications_$(sys.BUILDARCHSHORT)" After="InstallInitialize"
          Condition="VersionNT &gt; 400" />
    </InstallExecuteSequence>

    <!-- An earlier RecallCraft, and how it was installed: the program's App Paths entry, in HKLM
         for everyone on this PC, in HKCU for this person alone. (The registry view is the
         package's own, so an x64 package reads the 64-bit HKLM, where its earlier versions
         wrote.) -->
    <Property Id="RC_MACHINE_INSTALL" Secure="yes">
      <RegistrySearch Id="EarlierMachineInstall" Root="HKLM" Key="Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\App Paths\recallcraft.exe" Type="raw" />
    </Property>
    <Property Id="RC_USER_INSTALL" Secure="yes">
      <RegistrySearch Id="EarlierUserInstall" Root="HKCU" Key="Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\App Paths\recallcraft.exe" Type="raw" />
    </Property>

    <!-- An install in the other scope than the earlier one would not replace it (Windows upgrades
         only a product installed the same way) but sit beside it. A silent install that would do
         that stops instead. The context is per-user when ALLUSERS is empty, or still 2 with
         MSIINSTALLPERUSER set (Windows resets ALLUSERS=2 to 1 or empty as it decides). -->
    <CustomAction Id="InstalledForEveryone" Error="RecallCraft is installed for everyone on this PC, so this version can only be installed for everyone too (leave out ALLUSERS=2 MSIINSTALLPERUSER=1). To have it just for you, uninstall it first." />
    <CustomAction Id="InstalledJustForYou" Error="RecallCraft is installed just for you, so this version can only be installed just for you too (msiexec /i with ALLUSERS=2 MSIINSTALLPERUSER=1). To have it for everyone on this PC, uninstall it first." />
    <InstallExecuteSequence>
      <Custom Action="InstalledForEveryone" After="AppSearch"
          Condition="NOT Installed AND RC_MACHINE_INSTALL AND (NOT ALLUSERS OR (ALLUSERS = 2 AND MSIINSTALLPERUSER = 1))" />
      <Custom Action="InstalledJustForYou" After="InstalledForEveryone"
          Condition="NOT Installed AND RC_USER_INSTALL AND NOT RC_MACHINE_INSTALL AND NOT (NOT ALLUSERS OR (ALLUSERS = 2 AND MSIINSTALLPERUSER = 1))" />
    </InstallExecuteSequence>

    <!-- With the full UI, Windows looks for the version to replace (FindRelatedProducts) in the UI
         process, once, in the context it starts in: per-machine, the package's default. When the
         earlier install is per-user (and there is no per-machine one, which then wins), that
         context is switched to per-user first, so the earlier version is found and replaced; the
         first page then offers only "Just for me". AppSearch runs first to know. (ALLUSERS is
         emptied through a property that is never set: an empty ALLUSERS is per-user.) -->
    <CustomAction Id="LookForTheEarlierUserInstall" Property="ALLUSERS" Value="[RC_NO_VALUE]" Execute="immediate" />
    <InstallUISequence>
      <AppSearch Sequence="22" />
      <Custom Action="LookForTheEarlierUserInstall" Sequence="23"
          Condition="NOT Installed AND RC_USER_INSTALL AND NOT RC_MACHINE_INSTALL" />
    </InstallUISequence>

    <!-- Installer UI: WixUI_Minimal (progress, the finish page, repair and remove), with its first
         page (the license, whose Install button installs) replaced by the same page with two
         buttons, "Just for me" and "Everyone on this PC", which also decide the scope. Its
         dialogs and bitmaps are WiX's own (WixToolset.UI.wixext); package.ps1 builds the license
         RTF from LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE and the speech model's licence.
         "Just for me" sets ALLUSERS=2 and MSIINSTALLPERUSER=1 (as Microsoft's dual-purpose sample
         does) and points INSTALLFOLDER at %LocalAppData%\Programs\RecallCraft, where Windows puts
         a per-user install's ProgramFiles6432Folder: the UI process resolved its folders
         per-machine, and its INSTALLFOLDER is the one handed to the install and the one the finish
         page launches from. "Everyone on this PC" (with the administrator shield) sets ALLUSERS=1.
         When an earlier version is installed, only its scope's button is enabled.
         The finish page offers to start RecallCraft (ticked by default) the way a sign-in does
         (the same command line as the Run value), from the installer's UI process (as the person
         installing, not from the elevated install service), without waiting for it; silent
         installs (/qn) never show it, and RecallCraft then starts at the next sign-in. -->
    <WixVariable Id="WixUILicenseRtf" Value="$(var.LicenseRtf)" />
    <Property Id="WIXUI_EXITDIALOGOPTIONALCHECKBOXTEXT" Value="Start RecallCraft" />
    <Property Id="WIXUI_EXITDIALOGOPTIONALCHECKBOX" Value="1" />
    <CustomAction Id="LaunchRecallCraft" FileRef="RecallCraftExe" ExeCommand="--background"
        Return="asyncNoWait" />
    <UI>
      <ui:WixUI Id="WixUI_Minimal" />
      <Publish Dialog="ExitDialog" Control="Finish" Event="DoAction" Value="LaunchRecallCraft"
          Condition="WIXUI_EXITDIALOGOPTIONALCHECKBOX = 1 AND NOT Installed" />

      <Dialog Id="ScopeEulaDlg" Width="370" Height="270" Title="!(loc.WelcomeEulaDlg_Title)">
        <Control Id="Bitmap" Type="Bitmap" X="0" Y="0" Width="370" Height="234" TabSkip="no" Text="!(loc.WelcomeEulaDlgBitmap)" />
        <Control Id="Title" Type="Text" X="130" Y="6" Width="225" Height="30" Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="yes" Text="!(loc.WelcomeEulaDlgTitle)" />
        <Control Id="LicenseText" Type="ScrollableText" X="130" Y="36" Width="226" Height="124" Sunken="yes" TabSkip="no">
          <Text SourceFile="!(wix.WixUILicenseRtf)" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="LicenseAcceptedCheckBox" Type="CheckBox" X="130" Y="164" Width="226" Height="18" CheckBoxValue="1" Property="RcLicenseAccepted" Text="!(loc.WelcomeEulaDlgLicenseAcceptedCheckBox)" />
        <Control Id="ChoiceText" Type="Text" X="130" Y="188" Width="226" Height="40" Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="yes" Hidden="yes"
            ShowCondition="NOT RC_MACHINE_INSTALL AND NOT RC_USER_INSTALL"
            Text="Who is it for? Just for you needs no administrator and installs in your own folders. Everyone on this PC needs an administrator's permission." />
        <Control Id="MachineText" Type="Text" X="130" Y="188" Width="226" Height="40" Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="yes" Hidden="yes"
            ShowCondition="RC_MACHINE_INSTALL"
            Text="RecallCraft is installed for everyone on this PC, so this version replaces it there. Windows asks for an administrator's permission." />
        <Control Id="UserText" Type="Text" X="130" Y="188" Width="226" Height="40" Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="yes" Hidden="yes"
            ShowCondition="RC_USER_INSTALL AND NOT RC_MACHINE_INSTALL"
            Text="RecallCraft is installed just for you, so this version replaces it there. No administrator is needed." />
        <Control Id="BottomLine" Type="Line" X="0" Y="234" Width="370" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="JustForMe" Type="PushButton" X="114" Y="243" Width="76" Height="17" Text="Just for &amp;me"
            DisableCondition="RcLicenseAccepted &lt;&gt; &quot;1&quot; OR RC_MACHINE_INSTALL"
            EnableCondition="RcLicenseAccepted = &quot;1&quot; AND NOT RC_MACHINE_INSTALL">
          <Publish Property="ALLUSERS" Value="2" Order="1" />
          <Publish Property="MSIINSTALLPERUSER" Value="1" Order="2" />
          <Publish Property="INSTALLFOLDER" Value="[LocalAppDataFolder]Programs\RecallCraft\" Order="3" />
          <Publish Event="SetTargetPath" Value="INSTALLFOLDER" Order="4" />
          <Publish Event="SpawnWaitDialog" Value="WaitForCostingDlg" Order="5" Condition="!(wix.WixUICostingPopupOptOut) OR CostingComplete = 1" />
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Return" Order="6" Condition="OutOfDiskSpace &lt;&gt; 1" />
          <Publish Event="SpawnDialog" Value="OutOfRbDiskDlg" Order="7" Condition="OutOfDiskSpace = 1 AND OutOfNoRbDiskSpace = 0 AND (PROMPTROLLBACKCOST=&quot;P&quot; OR NOT PROMPTROLLBACKCOST)" />
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Return" Order="8" Condition="OutOfDiskSpace = 1 AND OutOfNoRbDiskSpace = 0 AND PROMPTROLLBACKCOST=&quot;D&quot;" />
          <Publish Event="EnableRollback" Value="False" Order="9" Condition="OutOfDiskSpace = 1 AND OutOfNoRbDiskSpace = 0 AND PROMPTROLLBACKCOST=&quot;D&quot;" />
          <Publish Event="SpawnDialog" Value="OutOfDiskDlg" Order="10" Condition="(OutOfDiskSpace = 1 AND OutOfNoRbDiskSpace = 1) OR (OutOfDiskSpace = 1 AND PROMPTROLLBACKCOST=&quot;F&quot;)" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Everyone" Type="PushButton" ElevationShield="yes" X="196" Y="243" Width="102" Height="17" Default="yes" Text="&amp;Everyone on this PC"
            DisableCondition="RcLicenseAccepted &lt;&gt; &quot;1&quot; OR (RC_USER_INSTALL AND NOT RC_MACHINE_INSTALL)"
            EnableCondition="RcLicenseAccepted = &quot;1&quot; AND (RC_MACHINE_INSTALL OR NOT RC_USER_INSTALL)">
          <Publish Property="ALLUSERS" Value="1" Order="1" />
          <Publish Event="SpawnWaitDialog" Value="WaitForCostingDlg" Order="2" Condition="!(wix.WixUICostingPopupOptOut) OR CostingComplete = 1" />
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Return" Order="3" Condition="OutOfDiskSpace &lt;&gt; 1" />
          <Publish Event="SpawnDialog" Value="OutOfRbDiskDlg" Order="4" Condition="OutOfDiskSpace = 1 AND OutOfNoRbDiskSpace = 0 AND (PROMPTROLLBACKCOST=&quot;P&quot; OR NOT PROMPTROLLBACKCOST)" />
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Return" Order="5" Condition="OutOfDiskSpace = 1 AND OutOfNoRbDiskSpace = 0 AND PROMPTROLLBACKCOST=&quot;D&quot;" />
          <Publish Event="EnableRollback" Value="False" Order="6" Condition="OutOfDiskSpace = 1 AND OutOfNoRbDiskSpace = 0 AND PROMPTROLLBACKCOST=&quot;D&quot;" />
          <Publish Event="SpawnDialog" Value="OutOfDiskDlg" Order="7" Condition="(OutOfDiskSpace = 1 AND OutOfNoRbDiskSpace = 1) OR (OutOfDiskSpace = 1 AND PROMPTROLLBACKCOST=&quot;F&quot;)" />
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Cancel" Type="PushButton" X="304" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Cancel="yes" Text="!(loc.WixUICancel)">
          <Publish Event="SpawnDialog" Value="CancelDlg" />
        </Control>
      </Dialog>
    </UI>
    <InstallUISequence>
      <Show Dialog="override WelcomeEulaDlg" Before="ProgressDlg" Condition="0" />
      <Show Dialog="ScopeEulaDlg" Before="ProgressDlg" Condition="NOT Installed" />
    </InstallUISequence>

    <StandardDirectory Id="ProgramFiles6432Folder">
      <Directory Id="INSTALLFOLDER" Name="RecallCraft">
        <Directory Id="MODELSFOLDER" Name="models" />
      </Directory>
    </StandardDirectory>
    <StandardDirectory Id="ProgramMenuFolder" />

    <Feature Id="Main" Title="RecallCraft" Level="1">
      <ComponentGroupRef Id="RecallCraftFiles" />
    </Feature>
  </Package>

  <Fragment>
    <ComponentGroup Id="RecallCraftFiles" Directory="INSTALLFOLDER">
      <!-- The program. Its shortcut starts it and opens its window, or opens the window of the
           one running. -->
      <Component Id="RecallCraftApp" Guid="838503DE-E263-4CA5-A848-AEB7F2BADEBD">
        <File Id="RecallCraftExe" Source="$(var.BinDir)\recallcraft.exe" KeyPath="yes">
          <Shortcut Id="StartMenuShortcut" Directory="ProgramMenuFolder" Name="RecallCraft"
              Description="Browse, replay and export what was said on your calls" WorkingDirectory="INSTALLFOLDER"
              Advertise="yes" Icon="RecallCraftIcon.ico" IconIndex="0" />
        </File>
        <RegistryValue Root="HKMU" Key="Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\App Paths\recallcraft.exe" Value="[#RecallCraftExe]" Type="string" />
      </Component>

      <!-- Started at every sign-in, for the person who installs it (HKCU in both scopes; see the
           top of this file): the same value the program writes itself when it first runs, and
           the one its own "Start RecallCraft when I sign in" switch turns off, by removing it. So
           the Run value is not this component's key path: Windows would repair a missing key path
           back (from the advertised shortcut), and the owner's switch would turn itself on again.
           The key path is a value of the installer's own that nothing else touches. Each person
           can also turn it off in Task Manager › Startup apps (StartupApproved, which the program
           reads). Both are removed on uninstall. -->
      <Component Id="StartAtSignIn" Guid="2F22BD12-4539-4BC4-BABB-F43F3BC10532">
        <RegistryValue Root="HKCU" Key="Software\RecallCraft\Installer" Name="StartAtSignIn" Value="1" Type="integer" KeyPath="yes" />
        <RegistryValue Root="HKCU" Key="Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run" Name="RecallCraft"
            Value="&quot;[INSTALLFOLDER]recallcraft.exe&quot; --background" Type="string" />
      </Component>

      <Component Id="RecallCraftCli">
        <File Id="RecallCraftCliExe" Source="$(var.BinDir)\recallcraft-cli.exe" KeyPath="yes" />
      </Component>

      <!-- The speech model that writes calls down (Whisper base.en, OpenAI, MIT; see
           assets/models/README.md), its licence and its readme, in models\ beside the programs,
           where they look for it. -->
      <Component Id="SpeechModel" Directory="MODELSFOLDER" Guid="544FEAB1-64DE-4D20-97CF-0EAF87692C55">
        <File Id="SpeechModelFile" Source="$(var.BinDir)\models\whisper-base.en-q8_0.gguf" KeyPath="yes" />
        <File Id="SpeechModelLicence" Source="$(var.BinDir)\models\LICENSE-WHISPER.txt" />
        <File Id="SpeechModelReadme" Source="$(var.BinDir)\models\README.md" />
      </Component>
    </ComponentGroup>
  </Fragment>
</Wix>
